IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `phi-cover`

-- Private Health Insurance Act 2007 (Cth) -- worked cases from the seat of the person deciding on hospital cover: ss 34-1,
-- 34-5, 34-10, 34-15, 34-20, 34-25, 37-1, 37-5, 37-7, 37-15, 37-20; ss 22-15, 22-20, 22-30, 22-40; ss 55-5, 55-10, 55-15;
-- s 102-1.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, the Lifetime Health Cover Rules or a government publication. Fixtures are generated by scratchpad
-- gen_private-health-insurance-act-2007_baseline.py; expected results were written by hand from the deposited text.
--
-- The life (workbench scenarios/au/wa): chloe c073 (2034-04-01), "Turns 31; hospital cover taken out before 1 July to avoid
-- the loading". Chloe Harding was born 14 March 2003, an Australian citizen by birth, so she turns 31 on 14 March 2034 and her
-- base day is 1 July 2034. Taking out cover on 1 April 2034, she has it on her base day: no loading. Her not being overseas on
-- that day is ASSUMED (the scenario does not say).
--
-- Every loading percentage relies on the INFERRED 2%-a-year formula (the s 34-1(2) and s 34-5(2) formulas are missing from the
-- deposit). Tier thresholds: every fixture uses $90,000 / $105,000 / $140,000, the s 22-35 figures "for the 2021-22 and
-- 2022-23 financial year", as ASSUMED stand-ins for the indexed figures, as the Medicare Levy Act baseline does.

